From dsh-fork-0002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ddv <ddvnguyen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:20:21 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fork(connection): opt-in fork.noAuth admits trusted-Host
 requests without a launch token

Default is stock: no token -> 401. With connection.fork.noAuth the Host fence
(trustedHosts) stays the gate: an untrusted Host is rejected 403, a trusted one
is admitted as the shared browser peer. Intended for a deployment behind an
external perimeter (Cloudflare Access); PROD never sets it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
